    'Citizens in Sri Lanka report problems with roads, waste collection, water supply, sanitation and public transport through phone calls, office visits and informal channels. Complaints are lost, nobody can see their status, and organisations cannot tell who is responsible or which complaints are overdue.',
    'CivicFlow is a role-based web application that gives every complaint a single, traceable digital lifecycle. A Citizen submits a complaint with a category, description, map location and optional evidence. The system routes it to the right department and automatically assigns the least-busy Officer. Officers review, prioritise, work on and resolve it, and every step is recorded in an append-only history that the Citizen can follow in an Updates inbox. Citizens rate the service after resolution. Administrators manage users, Officer invitations and service categories, dispatch complaints that are stuck in unstaffed departments, and monitor performance with analytics.',
